      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(nodes): resolve Unicode browser node names when configured by display name",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nBrowser gateway requests could fail to select a browser-capable node by display name when the node name used non-ASCII letters or numbers. The Browser gateway had its own ASCII-only matcher, while sibling node-selection flows use the shared resolver.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nThe shared node-name normalizer now preserves Unicode letters and numbers while still treating punctuation-only queries as unknown. Browser gateway node selection now goes through the shared resolver, and the shared resolver preserves the shipped compact selector form as a lower-priority display-name match so persisted selectors such as `MacStudio` still match `Mac Studio` without outranking exact display-name matches.\n\n## User Impact\nUsers can target browser nodes by Unicode display names without needing to copy a node id or IP address. Existing configured browser node selectors that omit spaces or punctuation continue to resolve after the gateway switches to the shared matcher.\n\n## Evidence\n- Claim proved at `c62de0bfb56de1df8338d12c946f11d43346cc1f`: Unicode display names are preserved, punctuation-only queries stay unknown, compact display-name selectors still resolve below exact display-name matches, and `browser.request` routes a configured compact Unicode browser node selector through the node proxy.\n- Focused tests: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/shared/node-match.test.ts extensions/browser/src/gateway/browser-request.profile-from-body.test.ts` passed with 2 Vitest shards, 21 tests passing.\n- Browser gateway proof: `extensions/browser/src/gateway/browser-request.profile-from-body.test.ts` now exercises `browserHandlers[\"browser.request\"]` with `gateway.nodes.browser.node = \"Café01\"`, connected display name `Café 01`, and observes `nodeRegistry.invoke` using `nodeId: \"cafe-node\"` with `command: \"browser.proxy\"`.\n- Runtime resolver proof: `node --import tsx --input-type=module -` importing `src/agents/tools/nodes-utils.ts` resolved `resolveNodeIdFromList([{ nodeId: \"cafe-node\", displayName: \"Café 01\", caps: [\"browser\"], commands: [\"browser.proxy\"] }], \"Café01\", false)` to `cafe-node`.\n- Diff hygiene: `git diff --check -- src/shared/node-match.ts src/shared/node-match.test.ts extensions/browser/src/gateway/browser-request.profile-from-body.test.ts` passed.\n- Review proof: `python .agents\\skills\\autoreview\\scripts\\autoreview --mode commit --commit HEAD` passed with no accepted/actionable findings.",
